# Secrets
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/

# Vector store — large regenerable binaries. data_level0.bin is already 17MB,
# and every re-ingestion rewrites the whole file into a brand new git blob.
# Rebuild with: python -m vector_store.vector_store
CHROMA_PERSIST_DIR/

# Personal scratch
notes.txt
check_quota.py

# Working issue list — raw findings, superseded by journey.md once written up.
OPEN_ISSUES.md

# Throwaway retrieval experiments and their scratch vector stores.
Scripts/exp_*.py
data/experiments/
data/uploads/

# Converted markdown. 1.4 MB of generated output regenerated from the PDFs in
# data/raw_pdfs/, which are themselves committed. Ignoring the output and
# keeping the input is the right way round: the PDFs are the source of truth
# and every re-conversion rewrites these files as new blobs.
#
# Consequence, recorded so it is not rediscovered later: a fresh clone has no
# markdown, so any build that starts from a clone must pay for conversion.
data/markdown_datalab/
data/markdown_datalab/
# NOTE: data/cache/*.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Those converted chunks
# cost 10-15 minutes of LLM calls against a limited daily free-tier quota to
# regenerate, and they are small (~200-280KB). They stay in the repo.

data\markdown_datalab
data/markdown_datalab/